cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: 'enigma-jev: a software Turing–Welchman Bombe with a probabilistic analyst'
abstract: >-
  A verified Enigma I, M3 and M4 simulator, crib dragging, a Turing–Welchman
  Bombe with the diagonal board and a ciphertext-only hill-climber. Jev, a model
  with typed probabilistic outputs, chooses cribs and judges trial decryptions.
  The software ships with a tiered backtest on historical intercepts, a
  validation of Bombe stop counts against Weinbaum (2025), and a comparison of
  Jev with n-gram judges and XGBoost. It includes two research notes: "Enigma,
  the Bombe, and a probabilistic analyst" and "A probabilistic analyst on trial".
authors:
  - given-names: Andres
    family-names: Godoy
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-09-28'
license: MIT
